2: 
3: Draft for independent mesh and grid adversarial reviews. This completes the
4: original-coordinate factory selection for bounded prepared draw/smooth programs.
5: Anchored grab, preview, dyntopo, general attributes, cavity and unbounded commands
6: remain separately gated; this slice does not weaken their guards.
7: 
8: ## Implementation
9: 
10: 1. Add a scratch-only prepared factory to each executor. Build the AccumLive
11:    manifest with a temporary Brush, then replace the command with a fresh
12:    AccumOrig instantiation when `nonAccum && accumulable && !relaxesBase`.
13:    Preserve neighbor dispatch. Do not invoke the live factory or publish extra
14:    defaults/declarations during capability queries or preflight. Do not append
15:    duplicate manifests when changing the execution template.
16: 2. Use this factory consistently in supportsResolved, single prepared execution,
17:    and every prepared program stage. Remove only the blanket nonAccum rejection.
18:    Keep all other capability gates and complete scalar/program preflight.
19: 3. Execute through the existing mesh/grid displacement, generation and capture
20:    paths. Non-accumulating DRAW uses stroke-start coordinates; relaxation stages
21:    remain live and preserve their existing base-adjustment behavior. Programs
22:    keep their separate capture slots and union of evaluated radii. No changes
23:    to raw factory behavior, saved brush flags, authored values or stack storage.
